draw((0,-1.7)--(5,2.7)--(-A,-A),dashed);[/asy] It is easy to determine the area of the region $E_3$, which doesn't suffer from the same problem. The graph of the region $E_1$ shows that a change of coordinates to $x - y$ and $y + z$ isolates the integral \[\int_0^1 (1 - x) dx,\]so the area is equal to $\dfrac{1}{2}.$ For the integral on the left (\(EE_2\)), coordinate change to $(x - y, z + y)$ isolates the integral on the right, \[2 \int_0^1 \left[ \frac{A - (1 - (1 - A))^2}{2} \right] dA = \frac{13}{16},\]so the area is equal to $\dfrac{13}{16 \times 2}.$ The graph of the region $E_4$ shows a change of coordinates to $(x - y, y + z)$ isolates the integral \[2 \int_0^1 \left[ \frac{(1 + A)^2 - 1^2}{B} \right] dA = \frac{2}{B}\]So the area is equal to $\dfrac{2}{B}.$
